    <innerclass refid="classStaffControllerBase" prot="public">StaffControllerBase</innerclass>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Type-erased interface for service-staff management operations. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>In plain words, this file lists the three jobs that deal with the people who work for a service entity (a clinic, pharmacy, etc.): Add a staff member, Remove a staff member, and Invite a staff member by email. &quot;Type-erased&quot; means the rest of the server can call these jobs without knowing which exact kind of service is behind them. Each job appears twice: an ordinary version that reports its result through a callback (a &quot;call me when you are done&quot; function), and an &quot;async&quot; version that uses a coroutine (a function that can pause and resume later). This file only declares the jobs; the real work lives in the class that inherits from it.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: This is the doorway the staff HTTP routes use to reach the concrete staff controller for any service type. Because the functions here are &quot;virtual&quot;, one route handler can serve clinics, pharmacies, laboratories and radiology centers alike — the call is automatically forwarded to the right object (selected with a <computeroutput>std::variant</computeroutput>, a variable that can hold one of several types). This file calls into nothing itself, but it is the contract that <ref refid="classStaffController" kindref="compound">StaffController</ref> implements and that the route registry depends on. Without it, managing staff would need separate route code for each entity type.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Virtual functions (calling the right version through a base pointer): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/virtual">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/virtual</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>C++20 coroutines (functions that pause and resume with co_await/co_return): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/coroutines">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/coroutines</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::variant (a type-safe union holding one of several alternatives): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/variant">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/variant</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
